  "scenario": {
    "name": "finetune-blur-cpu",
    "description": "Task 9.5 (CPU, so a small training set and few epochs, D36): fine-tune YOLO11n, the deployed CPU worker's model (D5), against blur, the drift that hurts the camera scenes most (9.2, E-051: -17 points of MOT17 mAP@50-95 at sigma 6). Training list v1 (configs/finetune.v1.yaml): 800 COCO train2017 images and ~790 frames of the MOT17 train sequences outside the eval, disjoint from the eval subset and the INT8 calibration set. One fixed configuration for both runs (10 epochs, batch 16, imgsz 640, Ultralytics' automatic optimizer, no mosaic, last epoch kept). Runs differ in one variable: blur-mix blurs a seeded half of the images (sigma drawn per image from 1 to 8 px at 1280 width, vms.drift.transforms), control blurs none, so the blur gain is told apart from the gain of training on camera scenes and MOT's box convention. Eval: detection subset v1, PyTorch (same mAP as ONNX Runtime FP32, E-046), clean, blur 3 and 6 (the target), and noise 25 (an untargeted drift); paired bootstrap.\n",
